  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Can You Build a Backyard Cottage on Your San Diego County Property?",
    "text": "Can You Build a Backyard Cottage on Your San Diego County Property?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "A backyard cottage can be a detached or attached ADU, but the exact requirements depend on the property’s jurisdiction, zoning, existing structures, lot dimensions, coastal location, fire exposure, utilities, and intended use. A building permit is required for an ADU, and the design must provide complete independent living facilities rather than simply adding an unfinished room.",
